.TH GTTY 1 "November 2026" "gtty 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gtty \- amateur radio RTTY terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gtty
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gtty
is a GTK4 RTTY terminal for amateur radio. It decodes Baudot RTTY from a sound
card with several parallel demodulators (matched filters with selectable modes,
a character correlator and optionally libcodec2) merged by a vote, skims the
whole passband, transmits by AFSK audio or true FSK keying
through a serial port, controls the transceiver with Hamlib, keeps an SQLite
logbook with ADIF export, reports to GridTracker2 over the WSJT-X UDP protocol
and offers an fldigi-compatible XML-RPC interface for logging programs.
.PP
All configuration is done in the Preferences dialog (Ctrl+comma). Settings are
kept in named configurations (as in WSJT-X), each a complete file under
.IR ~/.config/gtty/profiles/ ;
.I ~/.config/gtty/gtty.conf
records which one is active. The
.B Configurations
menu switches between them and clones, renames, resets or deletes the active one.
.PP
Station aids: a DX cluster band map with click-to-QSY, callbook lookup
(QRZ.com XML or HamQTH) with worked-before information from the logbook,
rig receiver filter width and IF shift controls, a Tune button, a CW
identifier and a TX monitor for FSK keying. All are set up in Preferences.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B F1 .. F12
Run the macro on that button.
.TP
.B Ctrl+T / Ctrl+R / Esc
Transmit, return to receive, abort.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Log the QSO.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gtty-cli (1),
.BR rigctl (1)
.PP
The user manual is at
.I https://github.com/gjyoung1974/GTTY/wiki
and in the
.I docs/
directory of the source tree; the Help item in the application menu opens it.
